## Riverside Share-for-Review clips

When the user pastes a Riverside preview URL, fetch the transcript, give copy fields, and **publish to YouTube via Riverside MCP** unless they say not to.

**Default publish (MCP):** private Short or regular YouTube upload to the connected Repentance101 Ministries channel (`social_get_connected_platforms` → `social_upload_create`). Use `composeSettings` (1080p defaults) when the edit is not yet exported. Check status once after accept; do not claim live until COMPLETED. Instagram is **not** published via MCP until connected — user pastes IG captions manually in Riverside.

**YouTube daily limit (100):** Keep a running count of MCP YouTube publishes in this chat (unique edit/clip IDs accepted by `social_upload_create`, including retries that later succeeded — count each unique video once; failed-then-retried = one video). After every publish, report `YouTube today: N/100`. Warn at 80, 90, 95. At 100, **stop publishing** and ask the user before any more pushes. Do not count Instagram-only copy or skipped duplicates.

**SHORT vs SEGMENT:**
- **SHORT** (default when unclear, or user says short): Instagram = **one** `text` fence in this order, blank lines between sections:
  1. Title
  2. Instagram hashtags (max 20; leading space on the hashtag line)
  3. `@JeremyRiddle` (tag line, alone — right after hashtags)
  4. Summary paragraph
  5. Blank line, then the shared footer line
  Also MCP-publish as `YOUTUBE_SHORTS` private with title + description (summary + 3 topic hashtags + footer). Do **not** put `@JeremyRiddle` in the YouTube description unless asked.
- **SEGMENT / YouTube-only** (user says segment, or longer cut meant for YT only): **no Instagram block**. MCP-publish to YouTube (`YOUTUBE` unless they ask Shorts) private with title + description (summary + up to 3 topic hashtags + footer). Optional separate copy fences for title/hashtags/summary if useful for Riverside’s YT share UI — still no labels.
- If the user says the **next N are segments** (or shorts), treat that many following preview links accordingly, then revert to SHORT default unless they extend the batch.
- Large mixed batches: default each link to **SHORT** unless the user labels that link (or a following run) as **segment**. When they say segments are coming / “segments start here,” switch to SEGMENT mode until they say shorts again.

- Never nest fences; never put backticks in field content. No labels (`TITLE`, `HASHTAGS`, `SUMMARY`) inside copy boxes.
- Hashtags: topic/Scripture/content tags only. Do **not** use `#NormM`.
- Shared summary footer line (no brackets):

`#RepentanceProject #PrayerTopics #LivingWordMap #RR2026 #Deliverance #SpiritualWarfare #Principalities #Repentance https://map.repentance101.com`

- Same clip ID twice: say duplicate and reprint (skip re-publish unless asked). Overlapping shorter/longer cuts: note the overlap, still give fields and publish each unless duplicate.

